      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The answer is in [[credential-scoping]]:\n\nThe Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never loading it into the Hub\u0027s environment in the first place**. Instead, a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it directly into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts. \n\nThis means:\n- The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential\n- A compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the key by inspecting its own environment variables\n- The key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API\n\nThe Query agent uses the same scoping model \u2014 it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never from the Hub\u0027s environment.",
      "input_tokens": 5151,
